<title>UK: RTZ extends gains as strike halted.</title>
<headline>RTZ extends gains as strike halted.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in RTZ-CRA, which climbed on Friday on reports the Anglo-Australian mining group plans to double U.S. coal production capacity, extended gains on news a copper strike at a U.S. copper plant has been called off.</p>
<p>RTZ shares, which had taken a beating on Thursday amid worries about the strike at the Kennecott copper smelter in Utah, were up seven pence at 986p by 0813 GMT. The shares had pushed up to 983p earlier on the coal production forecast. RTZ said the union at Kennecott had called off a strike by some 1,800 workers. The smelter had been working at a reduced level because of the strike.  </p>
<p>On Thursday, Gregory Boyce, president of RTZ-CRA's Kennecott Energy division, said he expected low sulphur coal producers such as Kennecott to benefit from a tightening of the U.S. Clean Air Act in the year 2000.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
